  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-PAK202</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workplace compliance through social dialogue and labour inspection promoted and facilitated</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on previous years of technical support, the ILO continues to strengthen labour administration systems in Pakistan by supporting institutional reforms, improving coordination between federal and provincial authorities, and enhancing data-driven governance. It advances more effective labour inspection through strategic compliance approaches, including risk-based targeting, inspector training, digital inspection tools, and stronger follow-up mechanisms to promote sustained compliance rather than one-time enforcement. The ILO also supports improved reporting and monitoring in occupational safety and health by helping labour departments develop more reliable OSH data systems, strengthen notification and recording mechanisms for injuries and diseases, and promote transparency in reporting. At the enterprise level, it encourages the adoption and scaling up of OSH management systems that align with international standards, strengthen prevention cultures, and promote meaningful worker participation, while addressing emerging risks such as heat stress and chemical exposure.
Similarly, the ILO builds on its scientific and evidence-based approaches to wage reform by providing technical assistance grounded in international labour standards. It supports governments and tripartite bodies to use ILO tools and methodologies for minimum wage fixing, wage impact assessments, and productivity analysis to ensure that wage-setting processes remain transparent, objective, and inclusive.</narrative>
  </description>
